$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: `load` (W, or VA with `apparent`) is required

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {"load": 0}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: `load` (W, or VA with `apparent`) is required

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {"load": -5}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: `load` must be a number from 0 to 1000000000, got -5

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {"load": "big"}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: `load` must be a number from 0 to 1000000000, got "big"

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {"load": 5000000}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: no conductor of the tables carries it: split the circuit

$ bimcraft-cli run --cmd 'circuit {"load": 1000, "method": "9"}'
[exit 1]
--- stdout

--- stderr
line 1 (circuit): circuit: `method` must be one of 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 11, 11A, 61, 61A, got "9"

